       [x] 59.9 Load-time false error state (reported: node red after loading a
             worksheet that had saved fine). pn-flow.c applies saved properties
             one at a time in file order, so reacting to bridge/from/to/amount
             synchronously judged the node deprecated before `last-update` had
             been restored, painted the error marker, and nothing repainted it
             afterwards -- red for good, despite a valid cached quote. The
             repaint and the refresh-kick now defer to a coalescing idle
             (bridge_quote_schedule_settle) that runs once the property batch
             is complete, and the kick is gated on cache_is_fresh so reopening
             a worksheet costs the provider nothing. Regression test
             load_order_no_error (verified failing without the fix).
             NOTE: PnRate has the IDENTICAL bug -- examples/crypto/
             exchange-rates.json loads red with status "Never updated" despite
             a saved rate + timestamp. Not fixed here; same shape of fix.
       [x] 59.10 Priced != swappable. The first cut hard-failed when PulseLN's
             STATUS[from]/PS[to] said a pool was closed. Verified against the
             live swap page: it gates only its *button* on PS[to] (outPool) and
             still displays the rate, saying "Swaps To BNB Temporarily Offline";
             same for an out-of-band amount ("Max Limit Exceeded"). A monitor
             that blanked its history whenever a pool drained would be useless
             exactly when it mattered, so the node now prices the route anyway,
             keeps success=TRUE, and reports the closure on `swappable` +
             `warning` + the status line. Limits float (PulseLN derives them
             from a USD band divided by the live price -- currently "$1 MIN,
             $1000 MAX"), so a node drifts in and out of range unattended;
             an out-of-band amount sets swappable=FALSE too.
             Rate verified against the rendered UI: the page showed 1.773281
             BNB for 100M PLS, the node computed 1.773277 in the same minute
             (0.0002% apart -- price drift, not formula error).
       [ ] 59.8 Deferred: more bridges (the enum + a build_request/parse branch
             per provider is the whole cost); a reverse quote ("how much PLS
