       [x] 76.2 The layout tables moved behind a descriptor (keys, cols, rows,
             width): pn_keypad_layout_get_keys() / _get_grid(), and the layout
             is now the first argument of pn_keypad_key_rect_in(). Adding a
             third pad is a table entry plus its key list.
       [x] 76.3 The Decimal Keyboard itself: 3x4, telephone order (1 2 3 on the
             TOP row, * 0 # on the bottom), the ten digits plus "*" and "#" as
             a new PN_KEYPAD_SYMBOL kind -> data.kind "symbol". No point, no
             operators, no clear keys. "*" is an operator on the calculator pad
             but a symbol here -- same code, different meaning.
       [x] 76.4 The node's WIDTH follows the column count (200 -> 152 px, same
             height), so the keys stay the same size on both pads; the painter
             gets the layout through PnKeypadPaintState, and a layout change
             drops the pressed highlight (indices name a different table now).
       [x] 76.5 Help page PnKeypad.html and the pipnode-nodes skill entry
             (sources.md) document both layouts and the "symbol" kind.
       [x] 76.6 Unit tests: the decimal table and its telephone order, the
